session:pr654Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #512 asked for the RDF encoding of DatatypeDefinition(DT DR) axioms (T(DT) owl:equivalentClass T(DR)), split out of #373. The module's own doc comment noted the right-hand-side DataRange can be complex, and named_data_range (the existing helper) only handled a plain named datatype, returning None for anything else -- exactly mirroring the state class_expression was in before #509 generalized it into a full complex-class-expression resolver. Rather than special-case DatatypeDefinition to only support named datatypes (which would leave the common case of e.g. DatatypeDefinition with a DataUnionOf or DatatypeRestriction on the right unsupported and skipped), named_data_range was generalized into an infallible data_range resolver covering all five DataRange variants via the spec's blank-node structural encoding, directly mirroring class_expression's shape. Since data_range is strictly more capable than the old named_data_range, it replaced it at every existing call site (DataSomeValuesFrom/DataAllValuesFrom, qualified data cardinalities, DataPropertyRange) rather than leaving two parallel resolvers -- this is a pure capability gain at those sites, not a behavior change for the named-datatype case they already handled. #650 (the most recent same-module precedent, property-chain axioms for #510) was read first and used as the template for doc-comment scope tracking, the skip()/triple_p_annotated() conventions, and test structure. One pre-existing test (data_restriction_with_complex_data_range_is_reported_not_silently_dropped) asserted the old skip-on-complex-range behavior and was rewritten to assert the new translated behavior instead, since its premise no longer held." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:654 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr654 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .
